  "Number": 12,
  "Question": "At \\(2{:}15\\) o’clock, the hour and minute hands of a clock form an angle of:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(30^\\circ\\)",
    "B": "\\(5^\\circ\\)",
    "C": "\\(22\\dfrac12^\\circ\\)",
    "D": "\\(7\\dfrac12^\\circ\\)",
    "E": "\\(28^\\circ\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The hour hand moves steadily between hour marks, so at \\(2{:}15\\) it has already moved beyond \\(2\\). Adjacent hour marks are separated by \\(360^\\circ/12=30^\\circ\\).\n\nThe minute hand points to \\(3\\). Since \\(15\\) minutes is \\(15/60=\\frac14\\) of an hour, the hour hand is one quarter of the way from \\(2\\) to \\(3\\). The smaller angle between the hands is the remaining three quarters of that interval:\n\\[\n\\frac34\\cdot30^\\circ=22\\frac12^\\circ.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice C.",
